# The dev/native aihu-compile binary (built by `cargo build --release -p
# aihu-compile` or copied here for local tests) is platform-specific and never
# committed. The published tarball ships only the ESM shim (bin/aihu-compile.mjs,
# committed below); the native binary arrives via the @aihu/compiler-<platform>
# optionalDependency packages.
bin/aihu-compile
bin/aihu-compile.exe
# Keep the committed ESM bin shim tracked (it is the `bin` target).
!bin/aihu-compile.mjs

# Cargo build outputs (native + cross-compiled targets).
target/

# wasm-pack output — built locally for benchmarks; CI builds it from
# source and publishes to GitHub Releases as aihu-compile-wasm.tar.gz.
pkg-wasm/

# SHA256 sidecars produced during local release-asset staging or
# verification. CI generates these and uploads them alongside binaries;
# nothing locally generated should ever be committed.
*.sha256
